cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  SalmonTE was developed by Jeong et al.; please cite their paper (preferred
  citation below). If you used this fork's changes (bug fixes, modern Salmon
  support or the per-locus index_loci mode), please also cite this software
  record.
title: "SalmonTE (sulevk fork): ultra-fast quantification of transposable elements, with per-locus mode and fixes"
abstract: >-
  Fork of SalmonTE, an ultra-fast and scalable quantification pipeline for
  transposable elements from RNA-seq based on Salmon. This fork adds support
  for modern Salmon versions, fixes FASTQ detection, condition ordering and
  error reporting in the statistical test, and adds an index_loci mode that
  quantifies individual genomic TE copies with coordinates.
